-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",314,{
[10017]="70008B84\n1\tBring Zaudru's crimson mandible to Atli Spider-bane\030Collect Zaudru's Crimson Mandible\tZaudru has made her lair in the caverns beneath the old dwarf-city of Helegrod, in the Misty Mountains. Atli Spider-bane is in the town of Archet, in Bree-land. Atli Spider-bane has told you the story of his encounter with Zaudru long years ago and has charged you with carrying out his vengeance.\n",
[10018]="70008B83\n1\tCollect Helegrod Shadow-brood Venom (total: 15)\tThe Shadow-brood spiders in the caverns beneath Helegrod possess the venom Atli Spider-bane is seeking. Atli is in the town of Archet, in Bree-land. Atli Spider-bane has asked you to collect venom from the Shadow-brood of Helegrod.\n",
[10019]="700228B4\n1\tDefeat ancient snow-beasts (total: 12)\tThe snow-beasts must be cleared from the paths of Helegrod for any assault to succeed against the Enemy holed up in the ancient dwarf-hold.\n",
[10020]="70000197\n1\tDefeat Bogbereth\tBogbereth hunts in the north-east reaches of Himbar, west and then north of Gath Forthnír. Lunathron cautioned you not to face Bogbereth with anything less than a fully-armed war-party. She must be defeated, lest she continues to spawn more of her foul brood.\n2\tTalk to Lunathron\tGath Forthnír is in the eastern part of Himbar, south and east of Torech-i-Bogbereth. Lunathron bade you destroy the great spider, Bogbereth. Now that she is no more, you can return to claim your victory.\n",
[10021]="700087E9\n1\tDefeat Captain-General Bordagor and claim the Grimwood Lumber-yard. You must not be defeated when the Captain-General falls\tThe Grimwood Lumber-yard is at the heart of the Grimwood Forest. Soldier Bagfra directed you to find your way to the Grimwood Lumber-yard and destroy the Elf-lord in charge of the enemy forces there.\n",
[10022]="700087E5\n1\tDefeat Captain-General Harvestgain and claim Lugazag. You must not be defeated when the Captain-General falls\tCaptain-General Harvestgain, a târk, leads the forces within Lugazag. Soldier Súmtharb made it clear that the only objective is to strike down the enemy's leader.\n",
[10023]="700087A6\n1\tDefeat Captain-General Lainedhel at Ost Ringdyr. You must not be defeated when the Captain-General falls\tOst Ringdyr is far to east beyond the Hoardale River and Tírith Rhaw. Task-master Krul directed you to make your way to Ost Ringdyr to slaughter the lord of the keep.\n2\tTalk to Task-master Krul\tTask-master Krul is at Gramsfoot. After storming the walls of Ost Ringdyr, you fought through the enemy and defeated the leader of the keep. You should return to Task-master Krul with news of his defeat.\n",
[10024]="700087E8\n1\tDefeat Captain-General Meldún\tHoarhallow is south of Gramsfoot. Soldier Dalgumthak directed you to Hoarhallow to kill the dwarf-lord in power there.\n",
[10025]="700087E7\n1\tDefeat Captain-General Mákan and claim Tol Ascarnen. You must not be defeated when the Captain-General falls\tTol Ascarnen sits on an island in the centre of the Hoardale River. You have been tasked with finding and slaughtering the dwarf-leader who now stands in command of Tol Ascarnen.\n",
[10026]="700087E6\n1\tDefeat Captain-General Verdantine and claim Tírith Rhaw. You must not be defeated when the Captain-General falls\tCaptain-General Verdantine is at Tírith Rhaw, far to the east and south, beyond the Hoardale River. Soldier Dahámab directed you to gather others and lay siege to the tower Tírith Rhaw in an effort to kill the leader of the forces there.\n",
[10027]="70008857\n1\tDefeat Gorgoris\tGorgoris, the brood-queen of the Grimfang, dwells somewhere within the Grimwood forest in Hithlad. First Marshal Núrdram asked you to find the brood-queen of the Grimfang and destroy her.\n2\tSpeak with First Marshal Núrdram at the Grimwood Lumber-yard\tFirst Marshal Núrdram awaits your return within the Grimwood Lumber-yard. You found and destroyed Gorgoris, the Grimfang brood-queen.\n",
[10028]="70022577\n1\tDefeat Grisgart and his drake-brood\tGrisgart, a Man of Angmar, strives to maintain control over the drakes of Helegrod and must be defeated before he can bring his terrible army to bear upon Rivendell.\n",
[10029]="70008B8A\n1\tCollect Cruel Helegrod Fang (total: 15)\tWorms and drakes have come to live within the central keep of Helegrod, the ancient dwarf-city in the Misty Mountains. Ormulf Worm-hunter is in Othrikar, in the North Downs. Ormulf Worm-hunter has tasked you with retrieving fangs from the drakes and worms that nest within the central keep of Helegrod. He has refused to offer you a reward for this expedition, insisting that the honour of the deed will be reward enough.\n",
[10030]="700228B5\n1\tDefeat Storvâgûn\tStorvâgûn, leader of the giants of Helegrod, has become corrupted by the forces of Angmar. His defeat will strike a terrible blow against the Iron Crown.\n",
[10031]="70008B7F\n1\tCollect Helegrod barter-sticks (total: 15)\tGiants in the service of Storvâgûn and his new masters can be found on the cliffs above Helegrod. Arifael is on Amon Nendir, south-west of Rivendell. Arifael has asked you to take the notched barter-sticks on which the giants recorded the wealth paid to them by robed Men of Angmar away from them. When you bring him enough of the barter-sticks, he will burn them.\n",
[10032]="7000889F\n1\tDefeat Golloval\tGolloval can be found south of the mine in an eagle-eyrie. Taskmaster Bárzqhosh tasked you with finding and slaughtering the eagle, Golloval.\n2\tReturn to Taskmaster Bárzqhosh at the Isendeep Mine\tTaskmaster Bárzqhosh awaits your return outside the Isendeep Mine. Golloval found his end at your will. You should return to Taskmaster Bárzqhosh with the news.\n",
[10033]="70064483\n1\tYou must overcome the evils gathered within Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel. NOTE: You must complete 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel' on any difficulty Tier to advance this quest. Once you have completed 'Discovery: Carn Dûm' by travelling to Bail Avarc, use the Instance Finder to join 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel'.\t\n2\tTalk to Grúmach at Bail Avarc\tGrúmach can be found at Bail Avarc in Angmar. You have overcome the masters of the Iron Crown in Gwathrenost and freed Angmar from their influence at last. You should talk to Grúmach. NOTE: Bail Avarc can initially only be accessed via stable-master routes. Bail Avarc can be reached via the stable-masters at Esteldín, Gath Forthnír, and the stables of Rivendell.\n",
[10034]="70008B8B\n1\tDefeat Ice Hatchling (total: 90)\tThe central keep of Helegrod is a spawning ground for ice-hatchlings. Ormulf Worm-hunter has asked you to defeat the ice-hatchlings that are spawning within Helegrod's central keep.\n",
[10035]="70008B8D\n1\tBring Mírdanant to Gonediad\030Collect Mírdanant\tThe dragon Thorog has been spotted behind the walls of Helegrod, Mírdanant still buried within his neck. Gonediad of Rivendell has asked you to try and recover the axe of Durin, lost in ancient battle with Thorog at Helegrod.\n",
[10036]="70008B91\n1\tDefeat Breosal\030Defeat Adhargal\030Defeat Grisgart\tGrisgart, Adhargal, and Breosal keep the forces of evil under control behind the walls of Helegrod. Lord Elrond has charged you with defeating the three Angmarim apparently keeping the evils within Helegrod under control and organized.\n2\tTalk to Elrond in the Last Homely House\tMaster Elrond is in the library of Rivendell. The three servants of Angmar within Helegrod have been defeated. Elrond should be told of your success.\n",
[10037]="700228C5\n1\tDefeat Zaudru and her brood\tThe Angmarim believe they control the spiders of Helegrod...they could not be more mistaken. The vile Zaudru is a force to be reckoned with by any.\n",
[10038]="70008B81\n1\tBring Storvâgûn's emblem of loyalty to Arifael\030Collect Storvâgûn's Emblem of Loyalty\tThe giant Storvâgûn is on the cliffs above Helegrod, the ancient dwarf-city in the Misty Mountains. Arifael is on Amon Nendir, south-west of Rivendell. Arifael has asked you to take Storvâgûn's emblem of loyalty away from him. Robed Men of Angmar gave the emblem to him in exchange for the service of the giants.\n",
[10039]="70008B8F\n1\tBring Helegrod Corcur talismans to Elladan\030Collect Helegrod Corcur Talisman (total: 6)\tThe Corcur of Helegrod can be found within its walls, far north of Imladris in the Misty Mountains. Elladan is at Thorenhad, his camp among the Bruinen Gorges west of Rivendell. Elladan has told you that each of the Corcur within Helegrod carry talismans from which they believe their strength comes. If enough of these talismans can be taken from their grasp, the will of the Corcur may be broken.\n",
[10040]="700608FF\n1\tThe Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found in the Clovengap in Mount Gundabad. NOTE: You must complete 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra' on any difficulty Tier to advance this quest. Once you have completed 'Discovery: The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra', use the Instance Finder to join 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra'.\t\n2\tCompleted\tYou have completed 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra'.\n",
[10041]="70008B90\n1\tBring Helegrod Angmarim emblems to Elrohir\030Collect Helegrod Angmarim Emblem (total: 7)\tAngmarim inside Helegrod, the old dwarf-city in the Misty Mountains, bear emblems that reveal their loyalties. Elrohir is at Thorenhad, his camp among the Bruinen Gorges west of Rivendell. Elrohir has asked you to defeat Angmarim inside Helegrod and take from them the emblems they carry.\n",
[10042]="7000135D\n1\tDefeat Ferndúr the Virulent\tThere are fell spirits in a ruined area not far from the Cauldron of Death in the central island of Imlad Balchorth. Ferndúr must be destroyed to disperse the evil threat in this cursed land.\n2\tTalk to Eiláf\tEiláf is back at Myrkworth, east from Ferndúr's lair. With Ferndúr slain, you should return to Eiláf to tell him the tale of your deeds.\n",
[10043]="70043BDB\n1\tSpeak to the Roving Threats Quartermaster of Central Gondor\tThe Roving Threats Quartermaster of Central Gondor asks you to band together and vanquish the Roving Threats of Central Gondor.\n2\tSpeak to the Roving Threats Quartermaster of Central Gondor\tThe Roving Threats Quartermaster of Central Gondor can be found in Central Gondor. You should speak with the Roving Threats Quartermaster of Central Gondor.\n",
[10044]="70043BDC\n1\tDefeat Abrakhòr\030Defeat Anbúrz\030Defeat Du-kalon\030Defeat Gundash\030Defeat Keterang\030Defeat Luruyak\030Defeat Render\030Defeat Ripper\030Defeat Scythe-jaw\tPush the Orkish forces further into the mountain.\n",
[10045]="70008B89\n1\tDefeat Thorog\tThe dragon Thorog has been seen atop the walls of Helegrod, in the Misty Mountains. Greip and Sigrun have seen Thorog from their small camp north of the source of the Bruinen and have charged you with his defeat.\n",
[10046]="700088C5\n1\tDefeat Tyrant Barashish and reclaim Tírith Rhaw. You must not be defeated when the tyrant falls\tThe Tyrant Barashish is at Tírith Rhaw, north of Glân Vraig, in the centre of the Coldfells. Sergeant-at-Arms Hesten at Glân Vraig directed you to seek out and defeat the Orc Tyrant, Barashish who holds command at Tírith Rhaw.\n2\tSpeak with Sergeant Hesten\tSergeant-at-Arms Hesten awaits your return at Glân Vraig. You defeated the Tyrant Barashish to reclaim Tírith Rhaw. You should return to Sergeant-at-Arms Hesten with the news.\n",
[10047]="700088C9\n1\tDefeat Tyrant Bûrzgoth\tGrothum is to the north of Glán Vraig. Sergeant-at-Arms Hafthor asked you to make your way to Grothum to defeat the troll-tyrant Bûrzgoth.\n2\tTalk to Sergeant-at-Arms Hafthor\tSergeant-at-Arms Hafthor awaits news of your victory over the Tyrant Bûrzgoth at Glân Vraig. You met the Tyrant Bûrzgoth at Isendeep and drove him from the mine. You should return to Sergeant-at-Arms Hafthor with the news.\n",
[10048]="700088C7\n1\tKill Tyrant Durgrat at Dâr-gazag. You must not be defeated when the tyrant falls\tDâr-gazag, built on the ruins of a Rhudauran citadel, lay far to the west of Ost Ringdyr, across the Hoardale River. Make your way to the fortress and defeat War-master Durgrat at this location. Sergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent directed you to kill the Uruk-warmaster Durgrat at Dâr-gazag.\n2\tSpeak with Sergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent at Glân Vraig\tSergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent awaits your return at Glân Vraig. Facing down the Enemy, you destroyed the War-master at Dâr-gazag. You should return to Sergeant-at-Arms Thurimbent with the news.\n",
})
